.TH "GLESHA-DOWNLOAD" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-download \- download an object from remote buckets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha download\fR KEY \-\-from REMOTE... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download the object KEY from the first remote in \-\-from that has it. The output file must not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-output FILE
Write to FILE (default: the last component of KEY).
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Remotes to download from, tried in order.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha download backups/documents.gpg \-\-from b2
glesha download backups/documents.gpg \-\-from b2,aws \-\-output documents.gpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-upload (1)
